 that the model does not predict mutation status.</p></fn><fn id="tbfnote5"><label/><p>A Manchester score of 10 for BRCA1 and BRCA2 or a combined score of 15 corresponds with a mutation probability of 10&#x00025; (<xref ref-type="other" rid="bib12">Evans <italic>et al</italic>, 2004</xref>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl4" position="float"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Area under the ROC curve (C-statistics) for each model</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th colspan="2" align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>95&#x00025; confidence interval</bold></th></tr><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Test result variable</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>C-statistics</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Lower bound</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Upper bound</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>BRCA1 models</italic></td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;Manchester</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.808</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.738</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.879</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x02003;BRCAPRO</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.802</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.731</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.874</td></tr>